  "summaries": {
    "en": "Badge selection, Wonder Seed hunting, and hidden exit routing for a complete Super Mario Bros. Wonder playthrough.",
    "ja": "バッジ選択、ワンダーシード収集、隠し出口ルートを解説するスーパーマリオブラザーズ ワンダー完全攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "platformer",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1580163661417-3606299e3f32?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Elephant Form is the most versatile power-up: it breaks blocks with the trunk, collects coins from a wider arc, and the water spray fills pipes—use it as your default form in exploration-heavy courses.",
      "Badges provide passive abilities that fundamentally change traversal—Parachute Cap (slow fall) enables approaches to Wonder Seeds placed above obvious platforms, while Boosting Spin Jump adds vertical reach for hidden block hits.",
      "Wonder Flowers trigger randomised stage transformations; the exit from a Wonder Flower sequence always leads directly toward the primary Wonder Seed. Follow the transformed environment logic rather than the pre-transformation map layout.",
      "In multiplayer, player bubbles can carry other players to safe ground—designate one player as the \"lifeline\" player who avoids danger specifically to rescue fallen teammates in difficult sections.",
      "The Special World courses require all Wonder Seeds from a world to unlock; prioritise collecting the secondary Wonder Seed (often in a hidden route) before clearing the main exit in each course."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ゾウの変身が最も汎用性が高い。トランクでブロックを壊し、より広い範囲でコインを回収し、水スプレーでパイプを満たす。探索重視のコースでデフォルト変身として使う。",
      "バッジはトラバーサルを根本的に変える受動能力を提供する。パラシュートキャップ（緩やかな落下）は明らかなプラットフォームの上に置かれたワンダーシードへのアプローチを可能にする。",
      "ワンダーフラワーはランダムなステージ変形を引き起こす。変形シーケンスの出口は常にプライマリワンダーシードに向かう。変形後の環境ロジックに従う。",
      "マルチプレイではプレイヤーバブルで仲間を安全な場所に運べる。1人を「ライフライン」役として難所での仲間救出に専念させる。",
      "スペシャルワールドのコースはワールド内の全ワンダーシードが必要。各コースのメイン出口前に必ず隠しルートのセカンダリワンダーシードを回収する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "World 1 Badge Unlock Priority",
        "body": "The first Badge Shop in World 1 offers three immediate choices. Prioritise the Crouching High Jump badge for the first 5 courses—it enables reaching hidden coin blocks and alternate exits that contain secondary Wonder Seeds. The Floating High Jump badge becomes more valuable from World 3 onward when vertical platforming challenges dominate course design. Complete the Badge Challenge rooms in each world as soon as they appear; these provide the rarest badges unavailable from shops."
      },
      {
        "title": "Wonder Seed Collection Basics",
        "body": "Every standard course has two Wonder Seeds: one at the primary Wonder Flower and one at the Goal Pole. Hidden exits exist in approximately 40% of courses—look for coin trails leading away from the main path, unusually placed pipes, and blinking tiles that indicate hidden blocks. The most reliable signal for a hidden exit is a path that requires a specific Badge ability (e.g., Boosting Spin Jump to reach a platform 3 tiles above normal jump height) that you haven't been prompted to equip."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Multiplayer Synergy in Tough Sections",
        "body": "In co-op, difficult platforming sections can be bypassed by strategic death: one player dies voluntarily, becomes a bubble, and is carried by a surviving teammate past the danger zone. The bubble player respawns with full HP at the exit. This strategy is legitimate and saves significant time in sections with instant-death hazards (lava, bottomless pits). The \"mole\" strategy—one player specialises in digging through dirt routes in Mole Madness courses—consistently outperforms individual exploration."
      },
      {
        "title": "Standee Multiplayer Benefits",
        "body": "In online multiplayer, other players appear as ghost Standees that can revive you when you press the action button near them. Place your own Standee at the hardest point of a course (the section just before the primary Wonder Seed) to help other players while earning friend-help points. Accumulating friend-help points unlocks special badge variations not available from shops. During World 4 and beyond, Standee placement becomes a collaborative tool for discovering alternate routes."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Special World and True Finale",
        "body": "The Special World contains 12 courses with dramatically increased difficulty. Each course requires a specific badge or power-up strategy not needed in regular worlds—read the course title screen badge icon before entering and equip accordingly. The final Special World boss requires collecting all Wonder Seeds from the Special World to unlock. After completing the Special World, completing all courses to 100% unlocks a bonus cutscene and a commemorative badge that modifies the ending credits sequence."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Rushing through Wonder Flower sequences without exploring the transformed area—Wonder sequences often hide secondary items (50-coin flowers, hidden pipe exits) that are only accessible during the transformed state.",
      "Using Fire Flower as a default power-up in puzzle-heavy courses—Fire Flower is damage-focused; Elephant Form, Drill Mushroom, or Bubble Flower solve environmental puzzles the Fire Flower cannot.",
      "Not checking for coin trail directions before committing to a path—coin trails always point toward either a hidden item or an alternate exit; a trail leading away from the Goal Pole always leads somewhere meaningful.",
      "Ignoring the Talking Flowers' hints—Talking Flowers provide direct hints about hidden exits and Wonder Seed locations specific to the course; listening to all three dialogue options reveals the best hint.",
      "Skipping Badge Challenges—Badge Challenges are the primary source of rare badges; skipping them before a difficult world means attempting those worlds without the optimal badge for the course design."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ワンダーフラワー変形中に急いで先に進む。変形中にしか取れないセカンダリアイテム（50コイン花、隠しパイプ出口）が変形エリアにある。",
      "パズル重視のコースでファイアフラワーをデフォルト変身として使う。ファイアフラワーはダメージ特化。ゾウ・ドリルキノコ・バブルフラワーが環境パズルを解ける。",
      "コインの流れの方向を確認せず進む。コインの流れは常に隠しアイテムか別の出口を指す。ゴールポールから離れる方向のコインの流れは必ず意味がある。",
      "しゃべるお花のヒントを無視する。しゃべるお花はコース固有の隠し出口とワンダーシードの場所を直接教えてくれる。全3つのセリフを聞く。",
      "バッジチャレンジをスキップする。バッジチャレンジはレアバッジの主要な入手先。難しいワールド前にスキップすると、コースデザインに最適なバッジなしで挑むことになる。"
    ]
  },
